#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90033e91-fdb2-5aa0-8cce-76762a38ffd2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arcsine"}] :question/id #uuid "f1eb9fd6-8927-54e9-bb01-57dd52871d59" :question/math-academy-id "e-386" :question/problem "Calculate the indefinite integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x = \\arcsin (x) + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7256d2e-7105-5a4e-8d0a-5e00dfc1e311" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arctangent"}] :question/id #uuid "7a798e77-3c04-51e3-adec-d695724ce450" :question/math-academy-id "e-387" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x = \\arctan{x} + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e6b5d85-0b53-580f-9520-6c33463231d5" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Inverse Trigonometric Functions and Some Manipulations"}] :question/id #uuid "6ff9c057-e61a-5648-9a49-72a70f3127bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-388" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {x^2+2}{x^2 + 1}\\,  \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1+1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2+1} \\textrm dx = \\arctan(x),\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063976 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67f41769-a0ff-5ecc-8b05-5890a7ac9fe3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arcsecant"}] :question/id #uuid "81e3df9e-e5ab-57ec-9a82-149a277e94f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-3890" :question/problem "If $f'(x) = \\dfrac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} - 2x,$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} \\, \\textrm dx = \\textrm{arcsec} \\, x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\text{arcsec}\\,(x)-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =5\\text{arcsec}\\,(x)-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90033e91-fdb2-5aa0-8cce-76762a38ffd2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using Arcsine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55427533-8f40-52aa-b9e7-bbca2fa08404" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286198} {:answer/id #uuid "d1fdcc9f